<FeatureFacts id="nutrition" />

Log food by searching, scanning a barcode or a nutrition label, or from your recent foods, recipes and
saved meals. Search doesn't need the exact name: word order, plurals, small typos and UK or US names
("mince", "ground beef") all find the same food. The barcode button is in every food search, including
when you add ingredients to a recipe. To look a food up without logging it, use the search button at
the top of the diary: scan or search, see its numbers for any amount, and star it for later.

Tap the calories card at the top of the diary to set your calorie and macro targets. If your coach sets
your targets, theirs are shown. Tap a meal's name to fold it away. Drag a food by its grip to reorder it,
or onto another meal (folded ones too) if you logged it in the wrong place. Each meal's ··· menu copies
a meal from another day, saves it as a meal to log again in one tap, or moves it to another meal.

Under the macros, the diary shows fibre, sugar, saturated fat and salt for the day. Tap All nutrients
for those plus 16 vitamins and minerals as a share of the UK and EU daily reference amounts, and tap one
to see which foods it came from. Plain foods (from the USDA and the French CIQUAL tables) carry vitamins
and minerals; packaged foods usually only list the label four, so the page says how much of your day it
covers. A new food takes the whole label in the order it's printed, and a recipe adds up its ingredients.

A recipe can be split into servings, or logged by weight: weigh the cooked food in the pot, and then log
the grams on your plate. Paste an ingredient list ("500 g chicken breast", "2 tins chopped tomatoes")
and each line is matched to a food for you to check. Your recipes, foods and saved meals are under My
foods (the book button on the diary).

With Pro, your custom foods, recipes, favourites and saved meals sync between devices, and the web
dashboard shows a week at a glance.
